        "body": "## Summary\n\n- keep brokered artifact reads signed by default even when a display base URL is configured\n- require an explicit public-read opt-in and isolate every public grant behind a random 128-bit capability namespace\n- expose the selected access policy in coordinator responses and document the secure migration path\n\nFixes https://github.com/openclaw/crabbox/issues/904\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm test --prefix worker` (808 tests)\n- `npm run format:check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run lint --prefix worker`\n- `npm run check --prefix worker`\n- `npm run build --prefix worker`\n- `go test -race ./internal/cli -run TestCoordinatorArtifacts`\n- `node scripts/build-docs-site.mjs`\n- autoreview: clean\n\n## Live proof\n\n- real Worker dry-run build completed with the production bindings\n- bucket-scoped Cloudflare R2 PUT/GET/DELETE canary remains an explicit pre-merge hold; the 24-hour, object-read/write, single-bucket credential form is prepared, but credential creation requires the owner confirmation mandated by the browser-control safety gate\n",
